  best candidate: radial profile at 0.940 pooled, retina 0.560, word 1.000.
  the channel-count control (retina at 12 coarse channels) pools at
  0.580. The candidate has to beat THAT, not just the 176-channel
  retina, or the finding is 'use fewer channels'.

  shapeprobe SAYS BUILD — a coherent visual front-end is worth building.
  This gates a build; it is not a result about the creature. It
  compares feature banks rather than what a brain makes of them, and
  it lets the candidates segment the frame, which the retina cannot.
  Both favour the candidates, so a REFUSE is decisive and a BUILD is
  a licence to measure.
