  shipped (1.00)         +115.6%
  relaxed (0.10)         +206.8%   (must be at least 1.2x the shipped gap)
  ablated (0.00)         +225.6%   (reported, not required. The
                         [normalisation] note's collapse-at-zero is about
                         central's SEPARABILITY, which is a different
                         observable — a wide rate gap here is no evidence
                         the ablated creature is a good one)

  PASS — the regulator costs real dynamic range and relaxing it
  returns some. Note what this does NOT say: the shipped gap is
  +115.6%, not nothing, so a rate-reading mechanism here is working
  against a narrowed signal rather than a flat one. An earlier
  reading of 2.8% came from `stpprobe` measuring its silent block
  first, on a creature whose regulator had not settled.
