  5 consolidation passes per arm, called directly rather than waited
  for; competition removes afferents under 0.50 of their target's mean

    arm       pruned   competed  % of     mean|w| in  mean|w| out change    min in  orphans 
    off       4043     0         19.1     0.13556     0.15138     +11.68    4       64      
    compete   10196    6153      48.1     0.13556     0.18358     +35.43    4       64      

  `change` is the mean |w| over surviving afferents after the passes
  against before, and the OFF ARM is its null — not 0%. Removing
  synapses at random would leave the mean where it was, but a
  consolidation pass also downscales every weight (§3.6), so the off
  arm's +11.68% is what a pass costs with no competition in it. The
  difference between the two columns is selection and the rest is sleep.

  off arm competed       0   (must be 0 — the control)
  competitive removals   6153   (must be > 0, or nothing was tested)
  selectivity            +35.43% against the off arm's +11.68%
  orphaned neurons       64 against the off arm's 64   (must not rise:
                             a stripped cell deletes the tract it was
                             meant to sharpen. Six are already there at
                             birth and are not this rule's doing)

  PASS — competition removes synapses the absolute floor did not,
  the survivors are stronger than the population it selected from,
  and no neuron was stripped.
